{#-
SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 Chris Su
SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

Copy to salt/config.local.jinja on the machine that renders Salt. That file
is gitignored and scripts/package.sh excludes it. Do not commit it, and do
not put it in the public deploy tarball.

This file is included by config.jinja after cfg is built. Mutate the dict
in place. Replacing a nested dict drops the keys you did not repeat.

AppVM tokens do not belong here. config.jinja is rendered on dom0, so a
value in this overlay is plaintext on dom0. Those tokens live in the private
sops checkout and are decrypted inside the AppVM. See salt/secrets/README.md.

The hotspot password is the dom0 exception: mgmt.hotspot reads it while
creating the NetworkManager connection. Leave it empty to skip creation.
An existing connection is left alone either way.
-#}
{% set _ = cfg['hotspot'].update({'password': ''}) %}
